From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergei Sveshnikov <sergei@svesh.dev>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:28:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] svesh: MCP for agents, drafts, service accounts, gentle IMAP
 sync, import

All changes of the svesh build in one patch; what each does is in README.md
("What the fork adds") of github.com/svesh87/bichon-patches.

- MCP at /mcp (BICHON_ENABLE_MCP): list_accounts, list_folders, sync_now,
  search_emails, get_email, get_thread, save_attachments, save_draft; nothing
  sends, deletes or moves mail. Drafts are APPENDed to \Drafts.
- Account permissions account:sync and data:draft; service accounts (users for
  API tokens only, POST /api/v1/service-accounts).
- Gentle mode for slow IMAP servers, per account: chunked body download, gap-fill
  by UID, folders without new mail skipped, waits before reconnects.
- Import into IMAP folders under server UIDs (/svesh-api).
- BICHON_LOG_FILTER: per-target log levels.
- Web UI for the above (account download settings, permissions, service
  accounts), en/ru strings; tests.
